📡 Telemetry

The CanSat Ground Control Dashboard receives real-time telemetry data from the CanSat via serial communication and displays mission parameters through an interactive LabVIEW NXG interface. All incoming telemetry packets are simultaneously logged into a CSV file for post-flight analysis.

Telemetry Parameters
Parameter	Description
CanSat ID	Unique identifier of the CanSat
Mission Time	Elapsed mission time
Packet Number	Sequential telemetry packet number
Temperature	Ambient temperature (°C)
Pressure	Atmospheric pressure (Pa)
Humidity	Relative humidity (%)
Satellite Count	Number of GPS satellites connected
Timestamp	Time of telemetry reception
Latitude	GPS latitude
Longitude	GPS longitude
Altitude	Altitude above sea level (m)
Battery Percentage	Remaining battery level (%)
Gyro X, Y, Z	Angular velocity from the IMU
Accel X, Y, Z	Linear acceleration from the IMU
Pitch	Pitch angle (°)
Roll	Roll angle (°)
Yaw	Yaw angle (°)
RSSI	Wireless signal strength
Camera Status	Camera ON/OFF status
Status Flag	Current mission phase (BOOT, ASCENT, DESCENT, LANDING)
Data Logging

Every telemetry packet is automatically saved in CSV format, enabling detailed post-flight analysis using software such as Microsoft Excel, MATLAB, or Python. The logged data includes environmental conditions, GPS coordinates, orientation, battery status, mission state, and communication information.
